<section class="section"><div class="shell">
  <div class="content-grid"><h2>Why this exists</h2><div class="content-body"><h3>The demo looks good. You still have a business decision to make.</h3><p>It can write the email. Summarise the call. Put the numbers in a report. But will any of that bring a customer back, save meaningful work or help you make a better decision?</p><p>You’re the one who has to approve the spend and live with the answer. A list of AI ideas isn’t enough.</p><div class="recognition-note"><p>For example: if good leads aren’t getting followed up, generating more of them may only create a bigger pile.</p><p>That’s an example of where I would look, not a conclusion about your business. First we need to understand what happens after the lead comes in, what gets missed and what that costs.</p></div><p>That’s how the Audit works. I review the business, look at the evidence and rank the opportunities. AI is one possible answer. It isn’t the starting assumption.</p></div></div>
  <div class="content-grid"><h2>What you get</h2><div class="content-body"><ul class="editorial-list"><li>A short form about your business</li><li>A review of sales, costs, daily work, decisions and useful data</li><li>Your best opportunities, ranked</li><li>The three I would act on first</li><li>An estimate of the impact when the evidence supports one</li><li>Clear advice on whether to build, buy or use a simple tool</li><li>A 90-minute call to go through the findings</li><li>A clear 90-day plan</li><li>What I would do if this were my company</li></ul><p>When the evidence supports a number, I will estimate the impact. When it does not, I will say so.</p></div></div>
